"""Hebrews — better covenant, rest, never forsake"""
from catalog._entry import e

ENTRIES = [
    e('Hebrews', 1, 3, 3, 'His Son is the radiance of his glory, the very image of his substance, and upholding all things by the word of his power, when he had by himself purified us of our sins, sat down on the right hand of the Majesty on high.', 'Upholds all; purified; sat down.', ['salvation', 'providence', 'glory'], ['guilty', 'hopeful'], ['radiance', 'upholding', 'purified', 'sat down']),
    e('Hebrews', 2, 14, 15, 'Since then the children have shared in flesh and blood, he also himself in the same way partook of the same, that through death he might bring to nothing him who had the power of death, that is, the devil, and might deliver all of them who through fear of death were all their lifetime subject to bondage.', 'Delivered from fear of death.', ['deliverance', 'fear', 'victory', 'salvation'], ['afraid', 'bound', 'hopeful'], ['death', 'devil', 'deliver', 'fear of death']),
    e('Hebrews', 2, 17, 18, 'He was obligated in all things to be made like his brothers, that he might become a merciful and faithful high priest in things pertaining to God, to make atonement for the sins of the people. For in that he himself has suffered being tempted, he is able to help those who are tempted.', 'Merciful high priest able to help the tempted.', ['mercy', 'compassion', 'strength', 'salvation'], ['tempted', 'weary', 'guilty', 'hopeful'], ['merciful', 'high priest', 'atonement', 'tempted', 'help']),
    e('Hebrews', 3, 6, 6, 'But Christ is faithful as a Son over God’s house. We are his house, if we hold fast our confidence and the glorying of our hope firm to the end.', 'We are his house; hold hope firm.', ['identity', 'hope', 'faithfulness'], ['insecure', 'hopeful'], ['house', 'confidence', 'hope', 'firm']),
    e('Hebrews', 4, 9, 11, 'There remains therefore a Sabbath rest for the people of God. For he who has entered into his rest has himself also rested from his works, as God did from his. Let’s therefore give diligence to enter into that rest.', 'Sabbath rest remains.', ['rest', 'peace', 'hope'], ['weary', 'anxious', 'peaceful', 'hopeful'], ['Sabbath', 'rest', 'people of God', 'diligence']),
    e('Hebrews', 4, 12, 13, 'For the word of God is living and active, and sharper than any two-edged sword, piercing even to the dividing of soul and spirit, of both joints and marrow, and is able to discern the thoughts and intentions of the heart. There is no creature that is hidden from his sight.', 'Living word; nothing hidden.', ['wisdom', 'truth', 'holiness'], ['confused', 'guilty', 'hopeful'], ['word', 'living', 'sword', 'discern', 'hidden']),
    e('Hebrews', 4, 14, 16, 'Having then a great high priest who has passed through the heavens, Jesus, the Son of God, let’s hold tightly to our confession. For we don’t have a high priest who can’t be touched with the feeling of our infirmities, but one who has been in all points tempted like we are, yet without sin. Let’s therefore draw near with boldness to the throne of grace, that we may receive mercy and may find grace for help in time of need.', 'Throne of grace; help in time of need.', ['mercy', 'grace', 'prayer', 'compassion', 'presence'], ['weary', 'tempted', 'afraid', 'guilty', 'hopeful'], ['high priest', 'infirmities', 'boldness', 'throne', 'grace', 'help', 'need']),
    e('Hebrews', 6, 10, 10, 'For God is not unrighteous, so as to forget your work and the labor of love which you showed toward his name, in that you served the saints, and still do serve them.', 'God will not forget your labor of love.', ['faithfulness', 'reward', 'love'], ['weary', 'unappreciated', 'hopeful'], ['forget', 'work', 'labor', 'love', 'served']),
    e('Hebrews', 6, 17, 19, 'God, being determined to show more abundantly to the heirs of the promise the immutability of his counsel, interposed with an oath, that by two immutable things, in which it is impossible for God to lie, we may have a strong encouragement, who have fled for refuge in laying hold of the hope set before us. This hope we have as an anchor of the soul, a hope both sure and steadfast.', 'Immutable oath; hope as anchor.', ['hope', 'promise', 'faithfulness'], ['anxious', 'afraid', 'hopeless', 'hopeful'], ['oath', 'impossible', 'lie', 'anchor', 'hope', 'sure']),
    e('Hebrews', 7, 24, 25, 'But he, because he lives forever, has his priesthood unchangeable. Therefore he is also able to save to the uttermost those who draw near to God through him, seeing that he lives forever to make intercession for them.', 'Able to save to the uttermost; forever intercedes.', ['salvation', 'presence', 'prayer', 'hope'], ['guilty', 'hopeless', 'afraid', 'hopeful'], ['forever', 'save', 'uttermost', 'intercession']),
    e('Hebrews', 8, 10, 12, 'This is the covenant that I will make with the house of Israel after those days, says the Lord: I will put my laws into their mind; I will also write them on their heart. I will be their God, and they will be my people. They will not teach every man his fellow citizen… for all will know me, from their least to their greatest. For I will be merciful to their unrighteousness. I will remember their sins and lawless deeds no more.', 'New covenant; laws on heart; sins remembered no more.', ['covenant', 'forgiveness', 'identity', 'wisdom', 'mercy'], ['guilty', 'hopeless', 'hopeful', 'loved'], ['covenant', 'heart', 'my people', 'merciful', 'remember no more']),
    e('Hebrews', 9, 12, 12, 'Nor yet through the blood of goats and calves, but through his own blood, entered in once for all into the Holy Place, having obtained eternal redemption.', 'Eternal redemption obtained.', ['salvation', 'forgiveness', 'eternal-life'], ['guilty', 'hopeful'], ['blood', 'once for all', 'eternal redemption']),
    e('Hebrews', 9, 14, 14, 'How much more will the blood of Christ, who through the eternal Spirit offered himself without defect to God, cleanse your conscience from dead works to serve the living God?', 'Blood cleanses conscience.', ['forgiveness', 'holiness', 'spirit'], ['guilty', 'shame', 'hopeful'], ['blood', 'cleanse', 'conscience', 'dead works']),
    e('Hebrews', 9, 27, 28, 'Inasmuch as it is appointed for men to die once, and after this, judgment, so Christ also, having been offered once to bear the sins of many, will appear a second time, not to deal with sin, but to save those who are eagerly waiting for him.', 'Will appear to save those waiting.', ['salvation', 'hope', 'forgiveness'], ['afraid', 'hopeful'], ['die', 'judgment', 'bear', 'appear', 'waiting']),
    e('Hebrews', 10, 14, 14, 'For by one offering he has perfected forever those who are being sanctified.', 'Perfected forever by one offering.', ['salvation', 'holiness', 'hope'], ['guilty', 'insecure', 'hopeful'], ['one offering', 'perfected', 'forever', 'sanctified']),
    e('Hebrews', 10, 16, 17, '“This is the covenant that I will make with them after those days,” says the Lord, “I will put my laws on their heart, I will also write them on their mind;” then he says, “I will remember their sins and their iniquities no more.”', 'Sins remembered no more.', ['covenant', 'forgiveness', 'mercy'], ['guilty', 'shame', 'hopeful'], ['covenant', 'heart', 'remember', 'no more']),
    e('Hebrews', 10, 19, 22, 'Having therefore, brothers, boldness to enter into the holy place by the blood of Jesus, by the way which he dedicated for us, a new and living way, through the veil, that is to say, his flesh, and having a great priest over God’s house, let’s draw near with a true heart in fullness of faith, having our hearts sprinkled from an evil conscience and having our body washed with pure water.', 'Boldness to enter; draw near.', ['presence', 'prayer', 'forgiveness', 'courage'], ['afraid', 'guilty', 'hopeful'], ['boldness', 'enter', 'living way', 'draw near', 'conscience']),
    e('Hebrews', 10, 23, 23, 'Let’s hold fast the confession of our hope without wavering; for he who promised is faithful.', 'He who promised is faithful.', ['hope', 'faithfulness', 'promise'], ['doubt', 'weary', 'hopeful'], ['hold fast', 'hope', 'promised', 'faithful']),
    e('Hebrews', 10, 35, 36, 'Therefore don’t throw away your boldness, which has a great reward. For you need endurance so that, having done the will of God, you may receive the promise.', 'Endurance; receive the promise.', ['endurance', 'reward', 'promise', 'hope'], ['weary', 'afraid', 'hopeful'], ['boldness', 'reward', 'endurance', 'promise']),
    e('Hebrews', 11, 1, 1, 'Now faith is assurance of things hoped for, proof of things not seen.', 'Faith: assurance of hoped-for things.', ['hope', 'faithfulness', 'wisdom'], ['doubt', 'anxious', 'hopeful'], ['faith', 'assurance', 'hoped', 'not seen']),
    e('Hebrews', 11, 6, 6, 'Without faith it is impossible to be well pleasing to him, for he who comes to God must believe that he exists, and that he is a rewarder of those who seek him.', 'God rewards those who seek him.', ['faithfulness', 'reward', 'prayer'], ['doubt', 'hopeless', 'hopeful'], ['faith', 'rewarder', 'seek']),
    e('Hebrews', 11, 11, 11, 'By faith even Sarah herself received power to conceive, and she bore a child when she was past age, since she counted him faithful who had promised.', 'Counted him faithful who promised.', ['faithfulness', 'promise', 'hope'], ['hopeless', 'doubt', 'hopeful'], ['Sarah', 'power', 'faithful', 'promised']),
    e('Hebrews', 12, 1, 2, 'Therefore let’s also, seeing we are surrounded by so great a cloud of witnesses, lay aside every weight and the sin which so easily entangles us, and let’s run with perseverance the race that is set before us, looking to Jesus, the author and perfecter of faith, who for the joy that was set before him endured the cross, despising its shame, and has sat down at the right hand of the throne of God.', 'Run looking to Jesus, author and perfecter.', ['endurance', 'hope', 'salvation', 'courage'], ['weary', 'ashamed', 'hopeless', 'hopeful'], ['cloud', 'run', 'perseverance', 'Jesus', 'author', 'perfecter']),
    e('Hebrews', 12, 5, 6, 'My son, don’t take lightly the chastening of the Lord, nor faint when you are reproved by him; for whom the Lord loves, he disciplines, and chastises every son whom he receives.', 'Whom the Lord loves he disciplines.', ['love', 'wisdom', 'holiness'], ['bitter', 'weary', 'loved', 'hopeful'], ['chastening', 'loves', 'disciplines', 'son']),
    e('Hebrews', 12, 10, 11, 'He disciplines us for our profit, that we may be partakers of his holiness. All chastening seems for the present to be not joyous but grievous; yet afterward it yields the peaceful fruit of righteousness to those who have been trained by it.', 'Peaceful fruit of righteousness afterward.', ['holiness', 'peace', 'wisdom', 'hope'], ['bitter', 'weary', 'hopeful', 'peaceful'], ['disciplines', 'holiness', 'peaceful fruit', 'righteousness']),
    e('Hebrews', 12, 28, 28, 'Therefore, receiving a Kingdom that can’t be shaken, let’s have grace, through which we serve God acceptably, with reverence and awe.', 'Unshakable kingdom.', ['kingdom', 'hope', 'grace'], ['afraid', 'anxious', 'hopeful'], ['Kingdom', 'shaken', 'grace', 'awe']),
    e('Hebrews', 13, 5, 6, 'Be free from the love of money, content with such things as you have, for he has said, “I will in no way leave you, neither will I in any way forsake you.” So that with good courage we say, “The Lord is my helper. I will not fear. What can man do to me?”', 'Never leave nor forsake; helper; no fear.', ['presence', 'provision', 'fear', 'courage', 'faithfulness'], ['afraid', 'anxious', 'lonely', 'money fear', 'hopeful'], ['leave', 'forsake', 'helper', 'fear', 'money', 'content']),
    e('Hebrews', 13, 8, 8, 'Jesus Christ is the same yesterday, today, and forever.', 'Christ unchanged forever.', ['faithfulness', 'hope', 'identity'], ['anxious', 'confused', 'hopeful'], ['same', 'yesterday', 'today', 'forever']),
    e('Hebrews', 13, 20, 21, 'Now may the God of peace, who brought again from the dead the great shepherd of the sheep with the blood of an eternal covenant, our Lord Jesus, make you complete in every good work to do his will, working in you that which is well pleasing in his sight, through Jesus Christ, to whom be the glory forever and ever. Amen.', 'God of peace; great shepherd; eternal covenant; complete you.', ['peace', 'covenant', 'guidance', 'calling'], ['weary', 'inadequate', 'hopeful', 'peaceful'], ['God of peace', 'shepherd', 'eternal covenant', 'complete', 'will']),
]
